          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "Fi Money Shuts Consumer Banking, Pivots to AI and Enterprise Tech After Co-Founder Gwalani Exits",
            "articleSection": "Job Evolution",
            "abstract": "Fi Money co-founder Sumit Gwalani has stepped down after six years, following the March 2026 shutdown of the neobank's consumer banking service and a broader strategic pivot toward AI and enterprise technology. The departure underscores the mounting pressures facing India's neobanking sector, where regulatory constraints on banking partnerships have made pure-play consumer neobanking increasingly difficult to sustain. The company's shift toward enterprise AI signals a growing trend of Indian fintech startups repositioning away from consumer finance toward B2B AI services.",
            "url": "https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/tech/startups/neobank-fi-moneys-cofounder-sumit-gwalani-steps-down-after-six-years/articleshow/130963885.cms",
